{"id": "EUVD-2026-81704", "enisaUuid": "76cb5666-746d-37ef-8241-671e32f79947", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nip6mr: do not clone dst in ip6mr_cache_report()\n\nIPv6 input attaches a non-refcounted (NOREF) dst to skbs under RCU.\nWhen an ingress multicast packet misses MFC lookup,\nip6mr_cache_unresolved() places the skb onto the unresolved queue,\nescaping the receive-side RCU grace period.\n\nIf the underlying route is deleted and freed, and the MFC queue is later\nresolved with a wrong parent interface, ip6_mr_forward() invokes\nip6mr_cache_report(..., MRT6MSG_WRONGMIF), which executes\ndst_clone(skb_dst(pkt)) on the freed dst entry, triggering a slab\nuse-after-free.\n\nReport packets queued to mroute6_sk (a raw socket) and netlink\nnotifications do not require an attached dst entry.\n\nFix this by:\n1. Removing dst_clone() in ip6mr_cache_report() and ensuring report skbs\n   do not hold a dst.\n2. Dropping skb_dst before queuing unresolved skbs in\n   ip6mr_cache_unresolved(), matching the fact that multicast\n   forwarding resolves outgoing routes anew via ip6_route_output().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:55", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f8287f606c8c028d4224e85d95dc448c6d6d623", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42ef371466d5648f5c9e8bc219f0af0a2c2bbf8c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f57b0fd1c62e1be274ee154ab7fb8ac4481b7f89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a674afaae4136c71943aa3e35d433676fd40e8f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/235b42b5860189eb8c27c36435ad932cae65a734"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90111", "GHSA-4329-5qmc-m43g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c01b6d2-6a3e-37b6-8761-0131cae77632", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67f415dd29063a5906c560051c00e42dcf01a4dd <235b42b5860189eb8c27c36435ad932cae65a734"}, {"id": "2d748deb-4540-356a-b78b-a11235403412", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "46b92172-3e66-346b-a3cc-8798ab3d55b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "549065c0-8551-3b20-aaee-a8f7cd85ed60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67f415dd29063a5906c560051c00e42dcf01a4dd <42ef371466d5648f5c9e8bc219f0af0a2c2bbf8c"}, {"id": "85cb9548-fd4a-3d06-baf7-d12b69e90d93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "98b9b339-63e5-340d-a861-311afa701c3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}, {"id": "a17fe63b-4c7c-3503-9818-8d4bf6db6659", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "d9a8b1ea-0b39-3f12-8f71-f8aba86ff61c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67f415dd29063a5906c560051c00e42dcf01a4dd <f57b0fd1c62e1be274ee154ab7fb8ac4481b7f89"}, {"id": "deaddb0c-5d22-3df0-89b8-1d07df51daf9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e26d12fb-1a3a-35d1-933d-6e1824a365a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67f415dd29063a5906c560051c00e42dcf01a4dd <7f8287f606c8c028d4224e85d95dc448c6d6d623"}, {"id": "e999bab1-3c4c-37fc-ba7f-8232b5f46ddb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67f415dd29063a5906c560051c00e42dcf01a4dd <4a674afaae4136c71943aa3e35d433676fd40e8f"}, {"id": "f61cbeed-2c3c-3815-bd16-ddc350b0f7d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "87a747d4-88a6-307c-ad5d-a8284c1fb9b5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExp